fix(failure): require a wall-clock floor before countSettled trusts a streak (#145) (#147)

crashSettleStableReads counted consecutive equal reads, not elapsed time: on
an unloaded machine 20 reads a millisecond apart can finish before a COMMIT
that is genuinely still in flight (RM-069, #90) has had a realistic chance to
land, so the crashed call's own delta could settle on a stale, too-low value.
That shortfall then surfaced as an apparent extra credential_issued once the
two replay issuances were added on top.

settleReads now also requires the streak to span crashSettleMinStableDuration
of real time, driven by a scripted clock in
TestMCP011SettleReadsHoldsAStreakForAMinimumRealDurationTooRM093 (MCP-011-C4),
which fails against the prior read-count-only loop for the expected reason
(reports 13, not the true 14) and passes with the fix.